// ESM COLD-RESOLUTION arm A (issue #134): a module whose only dependency IS mediated.
//
// #132 measured the ESM path's steady-state per-call cost. What nothing measured is the ONE-TIME
// cost of resolving a mediated specifier through the loader thread — the `resolve`/`load` hook
// round trip, the synthetic-module source generation, and `getEsmShim`. That cost is paid at
// startup, and the ESM path is on by default under the CLI.
//
// The harness imports this file under a fresh `?n=` query on every iteration, which is a distinct
// ESM cache key, so each import really re-resolves and re-loads — including this `node:fs`
// specifier, which capwall's `load` hook answers with a generated synthetic module rather than
// the builtin. `esm-cold-plain.mjs` is the same file with a NON-mediated specifier; the paired
// delta between them is capwall's synthetic-module work, with Node's own loader round trip (which
// both arms pay identically) cancelled out.
import * as fs from "node:fs";

/** Read once so the import cannot be elided, and so the harness can assert which object it got. */
export const boundReadFileSync = fs.readFileSync;
export const kind = typeof fs.readFileSync;
